      "content": "The right to repair is crucial because restricted access to repair information and parts forces consumers into costly, manufacturer-controlled repair ecosystems. This effectively creates monopolies where companies control not just the product, but its entire lifecycle. Furthermore, it increases e-waste significantly as consumers are forced to discard functional devices simply because repairs are deemed too difficult or expensive. Ultimately, this movement champions consumer autonomy and promotes a more sustainable, less wasteful technology future.",
